# SPRINT INTERVALS

Version 1.0

---

# Purpose

Sprint Intervals are repeated maximal or near-maximal running efforts separated by incomplete recovery periods to develop acceleration, repeated sprint ability and combat-specific anaerobic conditioning.

Within CAS, they are considered one of the highest-transfer conditioning methods for improving explosive locomotion and fatigue resistance.

---

# Philosophy

Combat is intermittent.

Athletes repeatedly accelerate, decelerate and recover.

Sprint Intervals develop the ability to repeatedly express maximal speed while maintaining movement quality.

CAS prioritizes sprint quality over training volume.

