# Success Criteria

The exercise is successful when:

Sprint times improve.

Acceleration becomes faster.

Movement quality remains high.

Recovery between sprints improves.

Transfer to combat explosiveness becomes measurable.

---

# Final Principle

Elite combat athletes do not move quickly only once.

They repeatedly accelerate,

recover,

and explode again.

Sprint Intervals develop this ability,

making speed sustainable throughout the fight.